# Template for devops/backup/.env-media-mirror (gitignored).
#
#   cp devops/backup/.env-media-mirror-example devops/backup/.env-media-mirror
#   $EDITOR devops/backup/.env-media-mirror
#   bash devops/secrets.sh minio minio-media-mirror devops/backup/.env-media-mirror
#
# Feeds the `minio-media-mirror` secret in the `minio` namespace, consumed by
# devops/backup/minio-media-mirror.yaml. See planning/media-abstraction.md §4.5
# and documentation/secrets.md.
#
# NEVER put a real credential in a committed file. This template carries
# placeholders only; devops/secrets.sh refuses to apply a file that still
# contains __FILL_...__, which is what makes an unsupplied endpoint a loud
# failure at apply time rather than a nightly job mirroring into nowhere.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE BACKUP TARGET -- REQUIRED, AND DELIBERATELY NOT DEFAULTED
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Any S3-compatible endpoint. NO CLOUD PROVIDER IS NAMED HERE OR IN THE CRONJOB,
# and none may be added: §4.1 requires that storage is reached over the S3 API
# and nothing else, so the provider is an operator choice and stays one.
#
# The single hard requirement is OFF-CLUSTER. A second bucket on this cluster's
# own MinIO shares the same disks and is not a backup -- media is unrecoverable
# by construction, we hold the only copy. The CronJob asserts this and refuses
# to run if the endpoint resolves back to this MinIO, but the assertion is a
# backstop, not the decision.
#
# Include the scheme. https:// is expected for anything off-cluster.
BACKUP_S3_ENDPOINT=__FILL_BACKUP_S3_ENDPOINT__

# The destination bucket on that endpoint. It must already exist -- `mc mirror`
# does not create it.
BACKUP_S3_BUCKET=__FILL_BACKUP_S3_BUCKET__

# Credentials for the target. Scope them at the target to write into that one
# bucket, mirroring what devops/minio-media-policy.json does on our side.
BACKUP_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=__FILL_BACKUP_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID__
BACKUP_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=__FILL_BACKUP_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY__

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE SOURCE (this cluster's MinIO) -- WRITTEN FOR YOU
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Filled in automatically by `bash devops/minio/media-svcacct.sh production`,
# which provisions the `media-backup` service account from the checked-in
# devops/minio-media-backup-policy.json. Read-only on the media bucket; it is a
# separate identity from the media-proxy's reader because `mc mirror` needs
# s3:ListBucket and the public read path must never have it.
#
# Do not fill these by hand -- run the script, so the credential in the cluster
# and the policy in the repo cannot drift.
SOURCE_S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
SOURCE_S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
